themselves by accident.

1654
01:15:05,833 --> 01:15:07,633
Maybe they should
cordon it off or something.

1655
01:15:07,667 --> 01:15:09,833
Yeah.

1656
01:15:09,867 --> 01:15:13,967
They should scratch his belly
till his leg shakes
to subdue him.

1657
01:15:14,000 --> 01:15:15,667
You're it!

1658
01:15:15,700 --> 01:15:17,533
Come on!
I tagged you!

1659
01:15:17,567 --> 01:15:19,833
[Solarite growling]

1660
01:15:19,867 --> 01:15:21,200
Sorry.

1661
01:15:23,067 --> 01:15:24,833
Hang on. I'm not quite--
okay, there we go.

1662
01:15:24,867 --> 01:15:26,733
[Screeching]

1663
01:15:29,033 --> 01:15:32,000
Good night, everybody.
Minneapolis rocks.

1664
01:15:32,033 --> 01:15:34,167
Big hand for the solarite band.
Come on.

1665
01:15:34,200 --> 01:15:37,833
♪ Shannon is gone, I see ♪

1666
01:15:37,867 --> 01:15:41,467
Huh. Next time
we're getting a cat.

1667
01:15:41,500 --> 01:15:45,033
Not a "dangerous" sign?
Rope it off? Anything?

1668
01:15:45,067 --> 01:15:47,300
Nope.

1669
01:15:47,333 --> 01:15:49,900
All dogs go to hell.

1670
01:15:52,000 --> 01:15:53,800
We're friends now. Why?

1671
01:15:53,833 --> 01:15:55,500
How's sessom?

1672
01:15:55,533 --> 01:15:57,133
He will be all right.
Liara's with him.

1673
01:15:57,167 --> 01:15:58,133
I'm glad.

1674
01:15:58,167 --> 01:16:00,300
You still wish to return
to your world?

1675
01:16:00,333 --> 01:16:02,467
- Yes, but--
- well, then, tonight's
the best time.

1676
01:16:02,500 --> 01:16:05,667
The chaos of battle
has brought us closer to
your moon than we've ever been.

1677
01:16:05,700 --> 01:16:08,133
- Really?
- It'll be a simple task
to maneuver rheton slowly

1678
01:16:08,167 --> 01:16:10,467
- ...and steadily even closer,
and the risk will not be great--
- it will?

1679
01:16:10,500 --> 01:16:12,633
- ...because the travel time
will be short.
- This is fascinating!

1680
01:16:12,667 --> 01:16:14,633
It will be well within
the range of the moon's radar?

1681
01:16:14,667 --> 01:16:16,967
- Yes, but we cannot
go unnoticed.
- Come on.

1682
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:19,633
- Now, as soon as we're within
range of your moon--
- okay.

1683
01:16:19,667 --> 01:16:22,467
- ...my men will carry
your suit out into the open.
- I gotta go fold some socks.

1684
01:16:22,500 --> 01:16:23,967
- If your people come
to investigate--
- this is riveting!

1685
01:16:24,000 --> 01:16:26,000
...we'll pull them
into our gravity
and direct their landing.

1686
01:16:26,033 --> 01:16:28,633
- Meanwhile,
you will enter your suit--
- wow. No!

1687
01:16:28,667 --> 01:16:31,800
...seal it up
so that you're not exposed
to our atmosphere, and...

1688
01:16:31,833 --> 01:16:33,667
- Well, the rest you know.
- This is fascinating!

1689
01:16:33,700 --> 01:16:35,467
- Where shall I meet you?
- In the control chamber.

1690
01:16:35,500 --> 01:16:38,000
- Someone will come for you.
- Wow.

1691
01:16:44,333 --> 01:16:46,833
I hogged out on a baby carrot.

1692
01:16:46,867 --> 01:16:49,133
I need to walk it off.

1693
01:16:49,167 --> 01:16:50,800
- Hi.
- Uh, get any better?

1694
01:16:50,833 --> 01:16:52,800
- Zetha.
- No.

1695
01:16:52,833 --> 01:16:54,167
It's you.

1696
01:16:54,200 --> 01:16:56,000
Yes, frank chapman.

1697
01:16:56,033 --> 01:16:58,000
- But you can talk.
- Son of a...

1698
01:16:58,033 --> 01:17:00,633
- Great.
- From my fright, when I thought
you were going to be killed,

1699
01:17:00,667 --> 01:17:02,633
something happened.

1700
01:17:02,667 --> 01:17:06,700
And after I screamed,
I found I was able to speak.

1701
01:17:06,733 --> 01:17:09,000
- Zetha...
- Hey, I'm talking here!

1702
01:17:09,033 --> 01:17:11,800
- I have many things to say
to you, frank chapman.
- Like "pickle."

1703
01:17:11,833 --> 01:17:14,367
It's so wonderful--
you being able to talk.

1704
01:17:14,400 --> 01:17:16,367
And I have so many things
to say to you.

1705
01:17:16,400 --> 01:17:17,967
Like "I think
we should break up."

1706
01:17:18,000 --> 01:17:19,633
Oh, everything
has been terrible.

1707
01:17:19,667 --> 01:17:22,667
Especially that lunch.
Ew. It was awful.

1708
01:17:22,700 --> 01:17:24,667
You're so lovely.

1709
01:17:24,700 --> 01:17:27,000
You have such
an adorable little face.

1710
01:17:27,033 --> 01:17:29,000
I think I'll jam
my tongue into it.

1711
01:17:31,000 --> 01:17:33,467
Boy, she is earning combat pay.

1712
01:17:33,500 --> 01:17:35,467
- Yep.
- Whoo.

1713
01:17:35,500 --> 01:17:40,367
And she's horrified
back into muteness.

1714
01:17:40,400 --> 01:17:43,467
- Isn't it strange?
- You haven't called
the police yet.

1715
01:17:43,500 --> 01:17:46,467
Here in this place,
I have found perhaps

1716
01:17:46,500 --> 01:17:48,200
what I've been looking for
all my life.

1717
01:17:48,233 --> 01:17:51,500
- Pancakes.
- And I must leave.

1718
01:17:51,533 --> 01:17:54,300
Although everything within me
wants to stay.

1719
01:17:54,333 --> 01:17:56,833
Especially my spleen.

1720
01:17:56,867 --> 01:17:59,000
It's my solemn duty to leave.

1721
01:17:59,033 --> 01:18:00,833
You understand that, don't you?

1722
01:18:00,867 --> 01:18:04,367
I'm sorry. Now I'm deaf.

1723
01:18:04,400 --> 01:18:06,633
Frank chapman,
I've been in love with you

1724
01:18:06,667 --> 01:18:09,000
- ...since the first time
I saw you--
- ew.

1725
01:18:09,033 --> 01:18:11,500
...and I've never been able
to speak a word of it
until now.

1726
01:18:11,533 --> 01:18:13,967
Is he a turnip
that grew a face?

1727
01:18:14,000 --> 01:18:16,867
But as I know,
my love for you is so strong.

1728
01:18:16,900 --> 01:18:19,133
I can overcome my revulsion.

1729
01:18:19,167 --> 01:18:22,833
So I also know
that you will leave.

1730
01:18:22,867 --> 01:18:25,133
I must leave.

1731
01:18:25,167 --> 01:18:28,200
Hang on.
I wanna get my gum back.

1732
01:18:28,233 --> 01:18:30,300
Mm. Well, I see
you've been flossing.

1733
01:18:30,333 --> 01:18:32,033
That's good.

1734
01:18:35,000 --> 01:18:38,467
The word "love"
means detest, right?

1735
01:18:38,500 --> 01:18:40,167
Wow, the first thing
I ever say in my life,

1736
01:18:40,200 --> 01:18:43,167
and I blow it big-time.

1737
01:18:43,200 --> 01:18:44,800
Look, it's over.
Leave me alone.

1738
01:18:44,833 --> 01:18:46,467
It's over!

1739
01:18:46,500 --> 01:18:48,067
[Equipment whirring]

1740
01:18:50,500 --> 01:18:53,033
- Good. You're on time.
- For once.

1741
01:18:53,067 --> 01:18:55,533
- [Herron] Here we go.
- Let me hear you say "yeah."

1742
01:18:55,567 --> 01:18:57,533
- [Whirring intensifies]
- Another hour,

1743
01:18:57,567 --> 01:18:59,833
and we shall be close enough
for you to be found.

1744
01:18:59,867 --> 01:19:02,867
I'm just gonna drop you off
at the bus station.
I hope that's okay.

1745
01:19:02,900 --> 01:19:04,500
[Whirring continues]

1746
01:19:04,533 --> 01:19:07,000
Don't. Don't.
You're smothering me.

1747
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:12,700
Delivery for robert downey, jr.

1748
01:19:15,200 --> 01:19:19,467
[Woman on radio]
Lunar base 1
to rocket ship 380. Over.

1749
01:19:19,500 --> 01:19:23,167
This is rocket ship 380
to lunar base 1. Over.

1750
01:19:23,200 --> 01:19:26,800
Radar has just picked up
a giant asteroid.
Identity unknown.

1751
01:19:26,833 --> 01:19:29,467
Cannot find any record of it
in the space charts.

1752
01:19:29,500 --> 01:19:31,300
The phantom planet.

1753
01:19:31,333 --> 01:19:33,867
Give us exact position
of asteroid.

1754
01:19:33,900 --> 01:19:36,333
Nine degrees
in northern cluster field.

1755
01:19:36,367 --> 01:19:38,333
And I have an order
from colonel lansfield.

1756
01:19:38,367 --> 01:19:40,367
You are to land
on this asteroid

1757
01:19:40,400 --> 01:19:42,300
and send white to investigate.

1758
01:19:42,333 --> 01:19:44,367
Immediately, young man.

1759
01:19:44,400 --> 01:19:46,533
I--

1760
01:19:46,567 --> 01:19:49,967
I hope you will find happiness
back with your people.

1761
01:19:50,000 --> 01:19:53,300
You would be my happiness...
If you were there.

1762
01:19:53,333 --> 01:19:55,800
You wanna live in my habitrail?

1763
01:19:55,833 --> 01:19:57,867
Frank chapman, please...

1764
01:19:57,900 --> 01:19:59,867
You must take this stone.

1765
01:19:59,900 --> 01:20:01,633
And rub it in your armpits.

1766
01:20:01,667 --> 01:20:03,833
It will be a good luck charm.

1767
01:20:03,867 --> 01:20:05,533
Hold on to it.

1768
01:20:05,567 --> 01:20:08,967
It will help you to go back
safely to your people.

1769
01:20:09,000 --> 01:20:10,467
Keep it.

1770
01:20:10,500 --> 01:20:12,533
Oh, she's gonna
"just friend" him.

1771
01:20:12,567 --> 01:20:16,800
And remember my-- my love.

1772
01:20:16,833 --> 01:20:19,667
Yes, zetha.
I'll keep it forever.

1773
01:20:19,700 --> 01:20:21,167
In my junk drawer
in the basement.

1774
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:25,800
I just confirmed it.

1775
01:20:25,833 --> 01:20:28,800
A rocket, similar to yours,
is heading in our direction.

1776
01:20:28,833 --> 01:20:30,967
- I hope they won't crash.
- Don't worry.

1777
01:20:31,000 --> 01:20:34,800
- It will.
- I have the best men
on gravitation control.

1778
01:20:34,833 --> 01:20:36,800
And I have another man
who's coming to help me

1779
01:20:36,833 --> 01:20:39,333
turn on the oxygen tanks
as soon as you're in your suit.

1780
01:20:39,367 --> 01:20:42,300
- [Tom servo mutters]
- Thank you, herron.

1781
01:20:42,333 --> 01:20:45,833
You know,
we've become friends here.

1782
01:20:45,867 --> 01:20:49,033
- Good friends.
- Which is why I bring up
my missing wallet.

1783
01:20:49,067 --> 01:20:51,500
We were
to become friends anywhere--

1784
01:20:51,533 --> 01:20:53,867
your planet or my earth.

1785
01:20:53,900 --> 01:20:55,300
[Groans]

1786
01:20:55,333 --> 01:20:57,133
I wish you and liara
much happiness.

1787
01:20:57,167 --> 01:20:59,833
This is longer than
a minnesota good-bye.

1788
01:21:01,567 --> 01:21:03,533
Um, don't call,
'cause I don't have a phone,

1789
01:21:03,567 --> 01:21:05,467
and don't write
'cause we don't have mail here.

1790
01:21:05,500 --> 01:21:06,867
And I don't have e-mail.

1791
01:21:06,900 --> 01:21:10,467
Look, I'm just really hard
to get ahold of.

1792
01:21:10,500 --> 01:21:12,800
Whew! I thought I was gonna see
that giant pink tongue

1793
01:21:12,833 --> 01:21:14,833
coming at me again.

1794
01:21:17,000 --> 01:21:19,633
Uh, a lot of animals
got in here,
used it for their toilet.

1795
01:21:19,667 --> 01:21:22,367
We tried to clean
most of it out.

1796
01:21:22,400 --> 01:21:24,200
Okay, in you go. Whoa.

1797
01:21:24,233 --> 01:21:26,467
Check this out.
He's nude!

1798
01:21:26,500 --> 01:21:27,833
Oh, man.

1799
01:21:29,367 --> 01:21:31,967
Just one more peek. Wow.

1800
01:21:32,000 --> 01:21:35,133
Whew. He almost stayed.

1801
01:21:35,167 --> 01:21:37,133
Oh-- oh, wait, wait, wait.

1802
01:21:37,167 --> 01:21:39,133
My thumb is bent back in here.
Ow! Ooh!

1803
01:21:39,167 --> 01:21:41,833
My leg is all twisted.
Ow! Ooh!

1804
01:21:43,500 --> 01:21:45,967
Yeah, the movie's circling
the drain at this point.

1805
01:21:46,000 --> 01:21:49,200
- Yep.
- I find you guilty as charged.

1806
01:21:49,233 --> 01:21:51,533
- [Women shouting] Kill him!
- [Tom servo mutters]

1807
01:21:51,567 --> 01:21:53,633
You'll never see
your world again.

1808
01:21:53,667 --> 01:21:55,500
Come on! We didn't like
these scenes the first time!

1809
01:21:55,533 --> 01:21:57,967
Yeah.

1810
01:21:58,000 --> 01:22:00,833
What if his flashbacks
lap themselves?

1811
01:22:02,833 --> 01:22:04,833
[Imitating goofy]
Can I go out, please?

1812
01:22:07,200 --> 01:22:10,533
Frank chapman,
I've been in love with you
since the first time I saw you.

1813
01:22:10,567 --> 01:22:13,533
No fair! You can't flashback
to stuff we saw 10 seconds ago!

1814
01:22:13,567 --> 01:22:15,200
Yeah.

1815
01:22:15,233 --> 01:22:17,200
Chapman. Chapman!

1816
01:22:17,233 --> 01:22:19,633
- You got any gum?
- White to beecher.

1817
01:22:19,667 --> 01:22:21,633
Come in, white.

1818
01:22:21,667 --> 01:22:23,200
I found chapman.
He's alive.

1819
01:22:24,733 --> 01:22:27,800
But there's no trace
of makonnen.

1820
01:22:27,833 --> 01:22:29,800
Where's makonnen?

1821
01:22:29,833 --> 01:22:32,367
He's dead. He's gone.

1822
01:22:32,400 --> 01:22:36,500
He kept yapping about beauty,
so I shot him out the air lock.

1823
01:22:36,533 --> 01:22:39,333
Oh, I am so jammed up
in my cup right now.

1824
01:22:39,367 --> 01:22:41,000
Oh!

1825
01:22:42,067 --> 01:22:44,700
Where are we?

1826
01:22:44,733 --> 01:22:46,800
Where are they?

1827
01:22:46,833 --> 01:22:48,533
Where are the others?

1828
01:22:48,567 --> 01:22:50,467
And where's waldo?
What about that whole issue?

1829
01:22:50,500 --> 01:22:51,633
Where's who?

1830
01:22:51,667 --> 01:22:52,867
Zetha.

1831
01:22:52,900 --> 01:22:54,800
What are you talking about?

1832
01:22:54,833 --> 01:22:58,300
Sessom, herron...

1833
01:22:58,333 --> 01:23:00,300
Man, you are nuttier
than an outhouse rat.

1834
01:23:00,333 --> 01:23:02,167
Come on.
Let's get back to the ship.

1835
01:23:02,200 --> 01:23:03,800
Hey, you wanna hear
something funny?

1836
01:23:03,833 --> 01:23:06,200
I found
a little dark-haired woman
on the bottom of my shoe.

1837
01:23:06,233 --> 01:23:07,367
[Chuckles]

1838
01:23:10,033 --> 01:23:11,833
White to beecher.

1839
01:23:11,867 --> 01:23:13,800
I'm bringing him in.

1840
01:23:13,833 --> 01:23:15,467
He seems to be all right.

1841
01:23:15,500 --> 01:23:17,467
He says makonnen is dead.

1842
01:23:17,500 --> 01:23:19,300
He keeps talking
about other people.

1843
01:23:19,333 --> 01:23:20,967
I think he's in
a state of shock.

1844
01:23:21,000 --> 01:23:22,333
Do you need assistance?

1845
01:23:22,367 --> 01:23:23,700
No, captain.
I can handle him alone.

1846
01:23:23,733 --> 01:23:25,967
Well, okay.

1847
01:23:26,000 --> 01:23:27,533
You know, frank,
you're a lucky guy.

1848
01:23:27,567 --> 01:23:29,800
You're going to
a nice federal prison.

1849
01:23:29,833 --> 01:23:32,033
This is a wandering planet.
Could've carried you anywhere.

1850
01:23:32,067 --> 01:23:34,533
East lansing, crab nebula,
oxnard.

1851
01:23:34,567 --> 01:23:36,167
I'm sure glad we found you.

1852
01:23:36,200 --> 01:23:37,533
'Cause we ran out
of ugly guys.

1853
01:23:37,567 --> 01:23:39,067
Zetha...

1854
01:23:40,700 --> 01:23:42,867
Where is she?

1855
01:23:42,900 --> 01:23:44,867
What you need is rest.

1856
01:23:44,900 --> 01:23:47,333
And a stern lecture
about letting your partner die.

1857
01:23:48,733 --> 01:23:50,667
So, were you small
when you were gone?

1858
01:23:50,700 --> 01:23:53,000
'Cause you're acting
like you were really small.

1859
01:23:55,000 --> 01:23:57,300
I just wanna remind you
this is a northwest flight,

1860
01:23:57,333 --> 01:23:59,300
so we'll be sitting
on the tarmac for an hour

1861
01:23:59,333 --> 01:24:01,633
with no beverages
and air conditioning,
and we're out of meals,

1862
01:24:01,667 --> 01:24:03,633
and the flight attendants
are overworked and abusive,

1863
01:24:03,667 --> 01:24:05,867
and if you complain,
we'll throw you off the flight.

1864
01:24:05,900 --> 01:24:08,033
[Equipment beeping]

1865
01:24:09,733 --> 01:24:11,700
Prepare for immediate takeoff.

1866
01:24:11,733 --> 01:24:13,367
I am preparing
for immediate takeoff.

1867
01:24:13,400 --> 01:24:16,800
You see me preparing?
Taking off air tanks
is preparing.

1868
01:24:16,833 --> 01:24:18,700
How do you feel, chapman?

1869
01:24:18,733 --> 01:24:20,133
I don't know.

1870
01:24:20,167 --> 01:24:22,300
I think I'm carsick.

1871
01:24:22,333 --> 01:24:24,133
I don't understand.

1872
01:24:24,167 --> 01:24:26,167
Why can't I have my sippy cup?

1873
01:24:26,200 --> 01:24:28,633
It's unbelievable.

1874
01:24:28,667 --> 01:24:31,633
[Beecher]
We'll get you back to moon base
for a thorough examination.

1875
01:24:31,667 --> 01:24:34,833
- And spanking.
- [Beecher]
Do you think you're hurt?

1876
01:24:34,867 --> 01:24:37,033
I don't think so.

1877
01:24:37,067 --> 01:24:39,200
[Beecher]
You must have been knocked out
for quite a while.

1878
01:24:39,233 --> 01:24:41,967
We hit you as hard
as we could.

1879
01:24:42,000 --> 01:24:44,200
I must have been dreaming.

1880
01:24:44,233 --> 01:24:46,867
Quite possible
you were delirious.

1881
01:24:46,900 --> 01:24:49,467
The shock of the crash-landing
of your ship.

1882
01:24:49,500 --> 01:24:50,833
Ray's gone.

1883
01:24:50,867 --> 01:24:53,300
Why don't we play the quiet game
when we take off, okay?

1884
01:24:53,333 --> 01:24:55,467
But I just left
zetha and herron.

1885
01:24:55,500 --> 01:24:57,367
They gave me rocks and stuff.

1886
01:24:59,200 --> 01:25:02,333
Well, I got a grisham novel.
I gotta get started on that.

1887
01:25:05,033 --> 01:25:07,667
I should have gotten her
a stick.

1888
01:25:09,167 --> 01:25:11,033
She had such
an adorable little face.

1889
01:25:11,067 --> 01:25:14,200
Yeah, well,
so does paul williams,
but you don't french-kiss him!

1890
01:25:14,233 --> 01:25:16,667
All rockets ready for firing.
Stand by for countdown.

1891
01:25:16,700 --> 01:25:18,200
You guys wanna see my rock?

1892
01:25:18,233 --> 01:25:20,533
The gravity of this planetoid
is very strong.

1893
01:25:20,567 --> 01:25:22,967
We'll need every bit of thrust
for our takeoff.

1894
01:25:23,000 --> 01:25:24,667
- Don't worry.
- I've got extra thrust.

1895
01:25:24,700 --> 01:25:26,133
I know we're gonna make it.

1896
01:25:26,167 --> 01:25:27,333
[Beecher]
Start your countdown.

1897
01:25:27,367 --> 01:25:29,333
- [White] Ten, nine--
- right.

1898
01:25:29,367 --> 01:25:30,967
- ...eight--
- yeah.

1899
01:25:31,000 --> 01:25:32,833
- ...seven, six--
- let's get on with it.

1900
01:25:32,867 --> 01:25:34,800
- Mm-hmm.
- ...Five, four--

1901
01:25:34,833 --> 01:25:37,500
- pi!
- ...Three, two,

1902
01:25:37,533 --> 01:25:38,800
one, zero.

1903
01:25:38,833 --> 01:25:39,967
[Rocket engine blasts]

1904
01:25:40,000 --> 01:25:42,200
And they die.

1905
01:25:42,233 --> 01:25:44,667
Houston, we have a moron.
Over.

1906
